cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "Chunking verdicts under count- and budget-matched retrieval: code, analysis plans and results"
abstract: >-
  Code, written analysis plans (pre-registration documents), deviation logs, run manifests and per-query results for a
  multiverse analysis of how the retrieval-selection protocol (a fixed number of chunks vs a fixed word budget) changes
  chunking verdicts in retrieval-augmented generation, with an extension to semantic chunking and dense retrieval,
  an exploratory answer-quality check and a provisional, single-coded protocol audit of recent chunking studies. The
  original version history is unavailable, so the timing of the analysis plans cannot be independently verified.
authors:
  - family-names: "Chand J C"
    given-names: "Swaroop"
repository-code: "https://github.com/swaroopchandrashekar13/research"
